    bottomLine:
      "A specialist: buy it for a genuinely tiny space or a shorter user, and rule it out otherwise.",
    description:
      "The Walker Pro is the smallest machine in this guide and the only one that offers any incline, a fixed 5% that does more for effort at 2 mph than an extra half a mile per hour would. That combination makes it a real option for a small apartment or an office nook where nothing else fits. The limitation is unavoidable and should be taken literally: a 34-inch belt suits shorter users, and anyone above about 5 foot 6 is likely to find their stride constrained. Treat height as a hard filter here rather than a preference.",
  },
  {
    id: "sunny-sf-t7971",
    name: "Sunny Health SF-T7971",
    editorialScore: 4.1,
    category: "Best 2-in-1 With Handrail",
    badge: "Best 2-in-1",
